1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,000
Every token launch asks you to trust that something is underneath the price. Usually, nothing is.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:19,000
We measured it on mainnet: 94 of the 100 newest tokens that graduated from Meteora's bonding curve had no permanently locked liquidity.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
This is Ballast: a Meteora launch with a floor you can see before the first public trade, and verify yourself.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,450
When a creator launches, Ballast computes the floor, F, from the launch parameters alone, and records it on-chain.

5
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:45,000
Every buyer sees their worst case up front, before anyone else can trade.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,230
Buyers trade on Meteora's Dynamic Bonding Curve until it graduates.

7
00:00:55,230 --> 00:01:02,360
85% of the raise migrates into DAMM v2 as two positions locked for good, owned by the program.

8
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:09,180
The other 15%, the migration fee, goes into a program vault and becomes one DLMM limit order resting at F.

9
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:16,000
Three Meteora products, one invariant.

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,500
Now let's try to break it.

11
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:34,700
Now we sell everything. Every token holders have.

12
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:49,140
The price slides down the pool's curve, lands on the floor, and the bid absorbs the rest.

13
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:57,500
The worst fill of the whole sell-out was 0.9984 of F, fees included. It's liquidity and a limit order; the program has no instruction that withdraws them.

14
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:13,620
Don't trust our app. One command reads the raw accounts and recomputes F with the same tested library.

15
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:18,820
Sixteen checks. Same answer, for anyone, every time.

16
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:23,500
And one command measures the floor under any Meteora pool on mainnet, today.

17
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:32,500
The page shows your worst case before you buy, and verifies it in your browser.

18
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:43,500
What this is not: late buyers can lose about 74%. F is in SOL. A sale straight into the DAMM v2 pool can execute below F. Not audited, not on mainnet yet.

19
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:54,000
Buyers see their worst case. Creators launch without being called a rug. Launchpads add one instruction. Ballast. Launch with a floor.
